        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): reject with AbortError when tool execution is cancelled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a tool execution is cancelled via the agent's AbortSignal, onAbortSignal calls run.kill() to terminate the child process - but the outer Promise resolved normally with the process exit code. The agent manager was misled into believing the tool finished normally.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe process exit handler (run.promise.then(...)) always called resolve(buildExecForegroundResult(...)) regardless of whether the exit was caused by an abort signal or natural completion. The onAbortSignal handler killed the child process but had no way to signal to the exit handler that the exit was caused by cancellation.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdded a `toolAborted` flag set by onAbortSignal before calling run.kill(). When the process exit handler fires, it checks this flag first and rejects with DOMException(AbortError) instead of resolving.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Cancel/stop during bash tool execution now correctly aborts the agent run instead of processing a dead process output\n- Backgrounded and yielded sessions remain unaffected (abort is skipped for those)\n- Prevents resource leaks from cancelled tool executions being treated as successful\n\n## Evidence\n\n### A. Unit Test Results (34/34 passed)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ exec backgrounded onUpdate suppression > suppresses onUpdate after abort signal fires\n ✓ ... (33 other tests)\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  34 passed (34)\n```\n\nThe key test `suppresses onUpdate after abort signal fires` validates that:\n1. Exec tool starts and produces output\n2. onUpdate fires once with initial output\n3. Inside onUpdate, abortController.abort() is called\n4. onAbortSignal fires -> disables updates + kills process\n5. The wrapper Promise rejects with AbortError (not resolves)\n6. After a tick, no further onUpdate calls happened\n\n### B. Code Flow (Before vs After)\n\n```\nBEFORE (bug):\n  onAbortSignal -> run.kill() -> process exits with signal\n  -> run.promise.then() -> resolve(buildExecForegroundResult)\n  -> agent run treats cancelled tool as successful execution\n\nAFTER (fixed):\n  onAbortSignal -> toolAborted=true -> run.kill() -> process exits\n  -> run.promise.then() -> check toolAborted -> reject(AbortError)\n  -> agent run correctly aborts\n```\n\n### C. Lint + Format\n\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts\n  No errors\n\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts\n  All matched files use the correct format\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts: +6 lines (toolAborted flag + AbortError rejection in exit handler)\n- src/agents/bash-tools.test.ts: +3/-1 (updated test to expect rejection)\n\nFixes #105681",
        "branch": "fix/bash-exec-abort-reject-105681",
